      "heading": "The substances on a real van",
      "html": "<p><strong>Solvents:</strong> in adhesives, cleaners, paint strippers and degreasers. Many catch fire and irritate skin and eyes.</p><p><strong>Adhesives and resins:</strong> isocyanate products, such as spray foam, are a leading cause of work asthma.</p><p><strong>Cleaning chemicals:</strong> bleach, descalers and caustic cleaners. Bleach mixed with acid can make toxic gas.</p><p><strong>Gases:</strong> flammable gases, refrigerants and confined spaces.</p><p><strong>Biological agents:</strong> Legionella, leptospirosis and other germs in contaminated spaces.</p>"
