      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>Who must follow the COSHH Regulations in the UK?</h3><p>Every employer and self-employed person whose work exposes people to hazardous substances. That includes cleaning chemicals, solvents, adhesives, gases and biological agents.</p><h3>What must a COSHH assessment cover?</h3><p>The substances, how people are exposed, and who is at risk. Also the controls, any PPE, health checks where needed, and what to do in an emergency.</p><h3>Is an assessment in the office enough?</h3><p>No. The Regulations say workers must get information, instruction and training. An assessment nobody has read protects nobody. It must reach the people it covers.</p><h3>Can a WhatsApp message prove an assessment was read?</h3><p>It can prove the worker said they read it. The message must name the assessment and the job. Quickler adds the time. That is stronger than an unsigned sheet filed months later. See <a href=\"/pages/risk-assessment-software-uk-sme.html\">risk assessment software for UK SMEs</a>, <a href=\"/pages/site-safety-inspection-uk.html\">site safety inspection software</a>, <a href=\"/pages/lone-worker-check-in-software-uk.html\">lone worker check-in software</a>, and <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler in any country</a>.</p>"
